                [ 'h2', 'CO₂ laser cutter specs that really matter' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Power and lens' ],
                [ 'p', 'Power determines how thick a material you can cut in one pass and how fast. The xTool P3 has an 80 W CO₂ laser. There is no single figure for the maximum thickness of acrylic or plywood, though – it depends on the material, lens, air assist and number of passes – so test your own material before you buy.' ],
                [ 'p', 'xTool sells 38 mm and 64 mm focal-length lenses for the P3. The shorter one gives a smaller spot for fine engraving; the longer one gives a greater depth of focus, which helps with thicker sheets.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Bed size and conveyor feeder' ],
                [ 'p', 'The P3 bed measures 914 × 457 mm: the bigger the bed, the more parts you nest on a sheet and the less often you handle material. For longer formats there is the Intelligent Conveyor Feeder for the P3. According to xTool, it extends the working area to 610 × 1300 mm, takes material up to 26 mm thick, clamps it and homes automatically, and shows a preview of the whole sheet with no blind spots. It is an automated version of what a passthrough does on many laser cutters, where you push long material through openings in the enclosure by hand.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Bed support: slats or honeycomb' ],
                [ 'p', 'The P3 comes with 17 metal slats, and up to 35 can be fitted. For sheets 1 mm thick or thinner, xTool recommends fitting all the slats so the material doesn’t vibrate or ripple. Slats reduce marks on the underside of thicker boards, while small parts and thin, flexible materials are better supported by the aluminium honeycomb panel for the P3, which is lightweight and rust-free. The panel and the conveyor are sold separately; the conveyor is also included in the P3 Versatile and All-in-one bundles.' ],
                [ 'products', '9089525088469,9181163585749' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Speed: read it with care' ],
                [ 'p', 'xTool quotes up to 1,200 mm/s for the P3 and up to 6,000 mm/s for the X1 with Hybrid Motion. These are maximum values that mostly matter for engraving; cutting thick plywood or acrylic is much slower and depends mainly on power. So compare the time of a whole job on your own file, not the numbers in a table.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Cameras, autofocus and auto-lifting base' ],
                [ 'p', 'In batch work, the time spent aligning each sheet adds up quickly. The P3 has four cameras for material positioning and safety monitoring, plus the ACS™ smart workflow: auto-positioning, autofocus, LiDAR distance measurement and an auto-lifting base. With the RA3 rotary it shows a 3D preview, and with the conveyor a preview of the whole sheet. The X1 has three cameras and AutoLift.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Enclosure and laser class' ],
