                [ 'h2', 'What does your workshop need before a CO₂ laser arrives?' ],
                [ 'ul', [
                    'Fume extraction. Cutting acrylic and plywood with an 80 W laser produces a lot of smoke. Ducting it outside through a short, airtight hose works best; where that is impossible, use a filtering air purifier. The xTool SafetyPro™ AP2 (150 m³/h) is designed for desktop machines and the AP2 Max (700 m³/h) for industrial-grade laser cutters; the AP2 Max comes in the P3 All-in-one Bundle and the AP2 in the X1 All-in-one Bundle.',
